---
source: tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"lint\", \"--help\"])"
---
Lint bundle hygiene: coded checks beyond conformance (orphans, drift, staleness)

Usage: okq lint [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --bundle <DIR>
          Bundle directory to query [default: current directory]

      --check
          Exit 3 if any finding survives the filters. For CI gating

      --json
          Emit machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of human-readable text

      --severity <LEVEL>
          Minimum severity to display

          Possible values:
          - error:   Errors only (`lint` never reports any)
          - warning: Warnings and errors
          - info:    Everything, including info-level findings
          
          [default: info]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also honors NO_COLOR)

      --rule <CODE>
          Report only this rule (repeatable, e.g. L9); conflicts with --ignore

      --ignore <CODE>
          Suppress this rule (repeatable, e.g. L11); conflicts with --rule

      --no-ignore
          Ignore all .okqignore files; query the full tree, nothing excluded

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  # Every hygiene finding (warnings and info)
  okq lint

  # Fail CI if anything is found
  okq lint --check

  # Drop the info-level rules (key order, self-link, unverified, draft)
  okq lint --severity warning

  # Only the orphan rule
  okq lint --rule L9

  # Everything except "no verified events" and "status: draft"
  okq lint --ignore L11 --ignore L12

  # As JSON, for CI or an agent
  okq lint --json

Lint is an opinion, not conformance: it never reports an error and never
changes what `okq validate` calls conformant. Rule codes are okf's; okf 0.2.7
renumbered them and moved the frontmatter and link rules into `okq validate`.
